{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n22 modules under `tests/unit/metrics/` (13 pairs), `tests/unit/workflow/` (3 pairs) and `tests/unit/reconciler/` (6 pairs: 2 in `diffing/`, 3 in `state/`, 1 at the package root) have a `<name>_heldout.py` twin. Once both oracles have been reviewed the split only doubles module count, duplicates identical helper definitions, and makes every rename touch two files. Across these 22 pairs no test-function name collides; 7 pairs carry helper/fixture/class definitions with differing bodies (14 definitions in all) and every other colliding definition is identical. The pair list with per-pair rename sets, filtered from enumeration (2) of the test-suite epic's first comment, is itemised in this ticket's first comment. Paths are stated at their post-rename name: the reconciler epic (friended-brainsick-degus) rename has LANDED, so `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` no longer exists and the modules live under `tests/unit/reconciler/`. All counts and paths in this plan were re-measured on origin/main ce5795c6a5c by listing `tests/unit/{metrics,workflow,reconciler}/` and AST-diffing every pair's top-level definitions, not sampled.\n\n## Approach\nDirectories: `tests/unit/metrics/`, `tests/unit/workflow/`, `tests/unit/reconciler/` — 22 pairs (13 metrics, 3 workflow, 6 reconciler — 2 in `diffing/`, 3 in `state/`, 1 at the package root). **14 definition renames over 7 pairs**, enumerated so the set does not have to be re-derived: `metrics/test_registry` (`_spec`); `metrics/test_event_metrics` (`_write_event`, `_ticket`); `metrics/test_git_metrics` (`_oracle_write_cap`); `metrics/test_sidecar_metrics` (`_review`, `_write`); `workflow/test_gate_error_sidecar` (`_OutageRunner`, `_gate_errors`); `reconciler/state/test_backend_scalar_surface` (`_backend`); `reconciler/diffing/test_canonical_outbound_equivalence` (`_jira`, `backend`, `_emit`, `_StubBindingStore`, `_ticket`). `reconciler/diffing/test_canonical_link_diff` was previously listed as a rename and is NOT one: its shared definitions are byte-identical, so it dedupes with no rename. For each pair: `cat` the held-out module into the base under a `# ── held-out oracles (merged from <name>_heldout.py) ──` divider; keep the base module docstring and append the held-out docstring's \"what it proves\" paragraph; dedupe identical definitions (`pytestmark` counts here — keep the base copy); rename differing definitions and repoint their callers; `git rm` the held-out file. Rename rule: suffix the HELD-OUT definition `_heldout` (e.g. `_load_heldout`) and repoint its callers; keep the base copy of identical definitions. The autouse fixture `tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_backend_scalar_surface{,_heldout}.py::_clean` has identical bodies: the merge keeps the base copy, so the base mechanism key survives and the held-out key buckets `stale`. No test body changes.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope: the 22 base modules under `tests/unit/metrics/`, `tests/unit/workflow/` and `tests/unit/reconciler/` named in the first comment and their 22 `_heldout` twins. Out of scope: the `tests/unit/` root pairs (S1), `tests/interfaces/` and `tests/integration/` (S3), `tests/scripts/` (S4), the 78 unpaired held-out renames (S5), every file under `src/`, and any test body change. `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` is in scope for the AC5 drain only.\n\n`tests/unit/review_bot/` was flagged as possibly unclaimed by any story in this epic. It is not: all 3 of its `_heldout` modules are **unpaired**, so they belong to `b721-6c6d`'s unpaired-rename pass, whose scope claims the 55 unpaired modules under `tests/unit/` *including its subpackages*. Nothing is added to this story.\n\n## Testing\n**Whole-tree deleted-filename sweep, before `make test`.** For each of the 22 removed `_heldout.py` basenames, `git grep -F <basename>` over the whole tree and classify every hit as a live reference (fix), stale prose (fix), or a frozen pre-fix literal (leave, and record it on this ticket). Sweeping only the merged pair is demonstrably insufficient: sibling story 361f-0a5c-bd12-463b broke four guard modules it never edited — a `parametrize` list, a nested-pytest node id, an AST-scan target path and a vocabulary allowlist entry — and its earlier pair-scoped run passed because a merged module never cites a sibling's path.\n\nMeasured on origin/main ce5795c6a5c, the live set for this directory set is **exactly one** hit: the `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` row `autouse_fixture::tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_backend_scalar_surface_heldout.py::_clean`, which the Approach covers and which the AC5 drain removes (the two `_clean` fixtures are byte-identical, so dedupe keeps the already-pinned base copy and the twin's key buckets `stale`). `scripts/criteria-vocabulary-allowlist.txt` pins none of these 22 paths, so this story does not touch it.\n\n**Match on the whole basename, not a substring.** A bare `git grep -F` over basenames over-reports: `test_attest_registry_heldout.py` contains `test_registry_heldout.py`, so twin `test_registry_heldout.py` appears to own a docstring reference in `tests/unit/test_attest_registry.py` that is in fact sibling 361f's to fix. Attribute every hit to its owning path before acting on it. `.test_durations` hits are excluded: it is a pytest-split sharding profile, tolerant of stale keys and exempt from the vocabulary gate, confirmed by 361f deleting 39 modules keyed in it with no resulting failure.\n\nPer pair: `pytest --collect-only -q <base> <heldout>` before and `pytest --collect-only -q <base>` after — counts equal (both recorded on this ticket); `pytest <base>` green. `make test` green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] No deleted filename is still referenced: for each of the 22 removed `_heldout.py` basenames, the WORD-ANCHORED `git grep -nE \"(^|[^A-Za-z0-9_])<basename>\"` returns no hit outside `.test_durations`, the `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` stale row named in Testing, and the one frozen literal recorded in the \"Frozen literals and the anchoring fix\" comment on this ticket (`tests/fixtures/dc_wiki_corpus/code_arrow.json:16`). **AMENDED 2026-10-31 — the original bare `git grep -F <basename>` could not satisfy this AC's own \"rather than matched as a substring\" clause.** `test_registry_heldout.py` is a literal substring of `test_attest_registry_heldout.py` (at index 7), which S1 `361f` left named in the provenance comments at `tests/unit/test_attest_registry.py:14,:84`, so the unanchored grep reports 2 permanent false hits that no implementation of this story could clear. Anchoring returns 0 for that basename while still finding the genuine `code_arrow.json` hit.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` **exits 0** and `python scripts/check_criteria_vocabulary.py` **exits 0**.\n- [ ] Zero paired twins remain in these directories: for each of the 22 pairs `git ls-files <base>_heldout.py` prints nothing (the unpaired `_heldout` modules in these directories are untouched here and renamed in S5).\n- [ ] Per-pair node counts reconcile: each merged base collects exactly the sum of the two prior counts, from the before/after `pytest --collect-only -q` runs recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` **exits 0** AND `pytest tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py` passes, with the stale `_clean` autouse row for the deleted `test_backend_scalar_surface_heldout.py` drained by `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale` and the shrunken baseline committed here. **AMENDED 2026-10-31 (2nd): the prior wording forbade `--update-stale`, contradicting this story's own `make verify` criterion.** `--check` tolerates a `stale` row, but `make verify` also runs `test_the_committed_baseline_matches_the_live_tree`, asserting `set(baseline) | admitted == live` exactly. `AGENTS.md` prescribes this drain and forbids hand-editing the baseline. Evidence: the \"AC5 contradiction\" comment. The earlier `new=0` amendment stands (bug `6f24-3d47-b251-4905`).\n- [ ] `make verify` green."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793501647895789641,"uuid":"b15737f0-f361-4f97-8b1f-71e6029313bc"}